2026-10-09T22:05:48.5665128Z [{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/pulls/30","id":4805067729,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUresus8AAAABHmeD0Q","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/pull/30","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/pull/30.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/pull/30.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/issues/30","number":30,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Make CI fail on real problems only: prove npm trust, gate releases on every check, and clear warnings","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #29.\n\nThe red \"Checks and release\" run on `main` ([37979761428](https://github.com/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/actions/runs/37979761428)) has the same cause as every release since the move to `link-foundation`. npm's trusted publisher still names `konard/disk-space-saviour`, so the OIDC exchange is refused and `npm publish` reports `E404 Not Found - PUT` (0.14.0, 0.14.1 and 0.15.0 all failed this way; 0.13.1 is still the latest on npm). The preflight printed `PASS` just before that failure, because it only checked that `ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_URL` was set.\n\n**A maintainer still has to do one manual step:** on npmjs.com → `disk-space-saviour` → Settings → Trusted publishing, change the repository to `link-foundation/disk-space-saviour`, keeping workflow `release.yml`. Until then the release now stops in Release Preflight with that explanation, not at the publish step. Once it is done, the missing GitHub releases are recovered for versions already on npm.\n\nThe cancelled \"Workflows\" run ([37627288421](https://github.com/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/actions/runs/37627288421)) was a one-off: it checked out the old `konard/` URL during the transfer, got a 403, and was cancelled. Later runs are clean.\n\n### What changed\n\nFalse positives (a check said green when it should not have):\n- Preflight proves npm trust with the package OIDC exchange, the same endpoint `npm publish` uses.\n- Releases need every check, including Docker-in-Docker, and never run after a cancelled job.\n- Registry checks bypass the CDN cache and treat a 5xx as \"unknown\", never as \"not published\".\n- Version and changeset guards diff against a verified merge base. An exact changeset move is not counted as a new fragment.\n- A missing GitHub release is recovered when the version is already on npm.\n- Runner images and tools are pinned (`macos-15`, `windows-2025`, secretlint 13.0.7, zizmor 1.30.1), and CodeQL is scoped to shipped code.\n- Changeset versioning is dry-run on pull requests.\n- The use-m interop test now runs on Windows. It used to skip unconditionally; the Windows Node and Bun legs now report `Loaded command-stream`.\n\nWarnings and errors:\n- The 22 root audit findings are cleared by upgrading Changesets 3, jscpd 5 and lint-staged 16.4.\n- The example app's 8 moderate advisories have no fix; they are now reported as a notice, where the summary used to look clean.\n- lychee walks the checkout by extension, so the `./**/*.html: No files found` warning is gone. Transient 429/5xx link failures are re-checked, and `RECHECK_VERBOSE=true` logs each probe.\n- The Deno use-m skip names the denied net permission; it used to claim the CDN was unreachable.\n- `deno.lock` is back in step with `package.json`, so Deno no longer re-resolves ranges on the runner. That re-resolution is what made Deno's 24-hour minimum dependency age reject `jscpd@^5.4.1` in this PR's first CI run. `tests/deno-lock.test.js` now fails whenever the two drift.\n\nMost fixes are ports from [js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template), compared file by file. The defects the template shares are reported as [template#219](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/219) (lychee glob warning) and [template#220](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/220) (Deno skip reason and lock drift). `docs/BEST-PRACTICES.md` §15 records the rules.\n\nThe analysis is in [`dev/log/issues/29/pulls/30/README.md`](https://github.com/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/blob/issue-29-607417a937bb/dev/log/issues/29/pulls/30/README.md), with the downloaded logs beside it. It covers the timeline, each requirement, root causes, and a verdict on every remaining warning (stubbed Docker echoes, CRLF, transitive deprecations, Changesets labelling npm notices as `error`).\n\n### How to reproduce and verify\n\n- Each fix has a test that fails on the old code, for example `tests/release-preflight.test.js`, `tests/deno-lock.test.js`, the lychee input tests in `tests/workflow-reliability.test.js`, `tests/transient-links.test.js` and `isWindowsFileUrlError` in `tests/use-module-integration.test.js`.\n- Local: `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`, `npm run check:duplication`, `bash scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`, plus the suites under Node (904 pass), `bun test --timeout 30000` (904 pass) and `deno test --allow-read` (746 pass).\n- CI on this branch is green on all five workflows.\n\nA patch changeset is included; the version is left to the release workflow.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-10-09T19:40:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T20:34:01Z","closed_at":"2026-10-09T20:33:59Z","merged_at":"2026-10-09T20:33:59Z","merge_commit_sha":"7c23a4aebf3dade3156952cb4c510c00931cefee","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/pulls/30/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/pulls/30/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/issues/30/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/disk-space-saviour/sta